Hi Claudia,

On 22 March 2010 at 17:13, Claudia Beleites wrote:
| Dear all,
|
| I'm wondering how to make the fact public that there is a bunch of R projects in
| the GSoC.
|
| Specifically,
|
| * Should we tell r-help?
| * r-devel can guess this, as there was the thread on the proposals and from
| there one can follow the link to the Wiki page. Still...

Fritz, Manuel and myself (eg: past and current GSoC / R admins) felt that
r-devel was more appropriate than r-help for this.  We are of course open for
discussion on this.  But for _hacking on R_ as the GSoC suggests: That really
is what r-devel focusses on.

| * should every mentor care about his project?

Not sure I understand the question, but I'd say yes. Who else would if not
the mentor who suggested it?

| * Would you consider _not_ sending an announcement to r-help as an appropriate
| filter: only students that are actively looking for GSoC will apply, thus saving
| us from "application spam"?

I think it tends to flow the other way: Folks seem to know about GSoC, look
at Google, find the R Project entry and then the wiki. I also blogged about this
which hit a few other sites via blog syndication, and that seems to lead
Google searches to it too.

That said, a little publicity may be a good thing, so if you want to draft a
post to r-help, why not?  Make sure to mention this list as the forum as I
wouldn't want to start a drawn-out discussion over there either.

Dirk

